WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Steelcase ranked first
in all four comparisons.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.900
Add a $400 ceiling, and
Branch appeared in every answer.

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.460
Same remote worker.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.820
Three different prompts.

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.360
Across 12 answers, Branch showed
up 12 times and Steelcase 11.

6
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.660
In the four numbered lists, all four
assistants put Steelcase first.

7
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.640
The price ceiling changed
how Steelcase appeared.

8
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.600
Gemini and Perplexity suggested
a used or refurbished Leap.

9
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.220
Claude named the Series 1
around the limit.

10
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.600
We captured suggestions
and estimates.

11
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.680
Prices and chair performance
remain unverified.

12
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.320
Try this for your brand.

13
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.300
Keep the shopper the same
and add your target price.

14
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.060
Then label each mention.

15
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.380
New, used or refurbished,
or over budget.

16
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.000
That tells you what the shopper
was actually shown.

17
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.020
Explore benchmark at
getrecoscope.com.
